  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe report door (PR #1798, issue #1696) opens `https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/new` in the browser, with the title, the body and the label in the query.\n\nThe body includes the Debug info report (#157). The \"Project:\" line of that report is the full path of the project file on the disk of the user. That path usually has the user name in it. The browser sends the path to github.com in the URL, and the user can publish it in the issue without notice.\n\n## Source\n\nFinding 1 of the review of PR #1798 at head `40d967840026f5cf2193d2d68537efcc4895bcae` (comment 7004545700). The maintainer ordered this follow-up when he ordered the merge.\n\n## What should happen\n\n- The report that the report door sends has the file name of the project only, not the path.\n- The Debug info report in the application can keep the full path, if it stays on the machine.\n- A test pins that the URL of the report door has no directory part of the project path.\n\nRefs #1696\n",
